## Third-Party Sources

The `ai/references/` directory contains Markdown extracts of publicly available
standards documents and reference materials, bundled with this library so the
`satops-time` agent can operate without network access. Each extract carries a
YAML frontmatter block with provenance (source URL, document ID, fetch date,
sha256 of source) and an attribution notice.

### CCSDS publications

The following CCSDS documents are included as text extracts of the official
PDFs published by the Consultative Committee for Space Data Systems
(<https://ccsds.org/>):

- CCSDS 301.0-B-4, *Time Code Formats* (Blue Book)
- CCSDS 502.0-B-3, *Orbit Data Messages* (Blue Book)
- CCSDS 503.0-B-2 Cor. 1, *Tracking Data Message* (Blue Book + Corrigendum 1)
- CCSDS 500.2-G-3, *Navigation Data Messages Overview* (Green Book)

Inclusion is per the CCSDS Reproduction Permission Statement
(<https://ccsds.org/publications/>): *"In general, reasonable reuse of materials
published in CCSDS documents is permitted with attribution, and reprint
permission can be provided in writing for those organizations that require
formal permission statements."* Organizations needing formal written permission
should contact <secretariat@mailman.ccsds.org>. The original CCSDS documents at
the URLs in each extract's header are authoritative; the bundled extracts are
derivative works for reference convenience.

### NAIF/JPL SPICE documentation

The bundled `naif-spice-time.md` is the *Time Systems Required Reading*
document from the NAIF SPICE toolkit (<https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/>). Inclusion
is authorized under NAIF rules
(<https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/naif/rules.html>), which permit redistribution of
SPICE documentation as part of third-party tools.

## Refreshing the Bundle

Run `scripts/update-references.sh` to re-fetch and re-extract the bundled
references. The script is idempotent (skips files whose source sha256 matches)
and is intended for maintainers updating the bundle, not for consumers of this
library.
